Z||000000||86SE||11-05-2001||12:37 AM||||I am stuck midway in my 3.4 conversion with two questions.<BR>- Can anyone give me the dimentions or measurements of the drill guide?<P>- What kind of adapter do I need for the oil pump?<P>If anyone has a starter drill guide I could borrow I would really appreciate it.<P><BR>Thanks,<BR>Chuck<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg">     <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>V-6 w/rod knock Yellow Fiero<BR> -- 3.4L Conversion *Back in session!* --||||reg||1
Z||000001||Nashco||11-05-2001||02:03 AM||||I'd really like it if somebody could supply measurements for the "new" starter holes as well.  I have access to the equipment to drill the holes, don't need the expensive jig, just measurements of what it is.  Thanks in advance!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||11-06-2001||08:16 AM||||Just measure the center to center distance of the holes on the starter.||||reg||1
Z||000003||redfiero||11-06-2001||11:10 AM||||I just relocated the starter on my 3.4.  I used the starter as the template.  It was pretty hard to do.  I would suggest renting a template from someone (providing that the template has drill bushings in it).  The hole that is the farthest outboard has to be drilled into the chamfer on the block.  Its tough with a hand drill and no template.<P>Have you test fit your 2.8 oil pan onto your 3.4?  I put mine on and most of the holes didn't line up.  I'm going to use the 3.4 oil pan and oil pump.<P>matt||||reg||1
